---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelModelFeaturesConfig
---@field frequentlyBoughtTogetherConfig? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelFrequentlyBoughtTogetherFeaturesConfig Additional configs for frequently-bought-together models.

---The PageOptimizationConfig for model training. This determines how many panels to optimize for, and which serving configs to consider for each panel. The purpose of this model is to optimize which ServingConfig to show on which panels in way that optimizes the visitors shopping journey.
---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfig
---@field panels? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigPanelList Required. A list of panel configurations. Limit = 5.
---@field pageOptimizationEventType? string Required. The type of UserEvent this page optimization is shown for. Each page has an associated event type - this will be the corresponding event type for the page that the page optimization model is used on. Supported types: * `add-to-cart`: Products being added to cart. * `detail-page-view`: Products detail page viewed. * `home-page-view`: Homepage viewed * `category-page-view`: Homepage viewed * `shopping-cart-page-view`: User viewing a shopping cart. `home-page-view` only allows models with type `recommended-for-you`. All other page_optimization_event_type allow all Model.types.
---@field restriction? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigRestrictionEnum|string Optional. How to restrict results across panels e.g. can the same ServingConfig be shown on multiple panels at once. If unspecified, default to `UNIQUE_MODEL_RESTRICTION`.

---A candidate to consider for a given panel. Currently only ServingConfig are valid candidates.
---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigCandidate
---@field servingConfigId? string This has to be a valid ServingConfig identifier. For example, for a ServingConfig with full name: `projects/*/locations/global/catalogs/default_catalog/servingConfigs/my_candidate_config`, this would be `my_candidate_config`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigCandidateList gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigCandidate[]

---An individual panel with a list of ServingConfigs to consider for it.
---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigPanel
---@field candidates? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigCandidateList Required. The candidates to consider on the panel.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The name to display for the panel.
---@field defaultCandidate? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigCandidate Required. The default candidate. If the model fails at serving time, we fall back to the default.

---@alias gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigPanelList gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigPanel[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPageOptimizationConfigRestrictionEnum "RESTRICTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_RESTRICTION"|"UNIQUE_SERVING_CONFIG_RESTRICTION"|"UNIQUE_MODEL_RESTRICTION"|"UNIQUE_MODEL_TYPE_RESTRICTION"

---@alias gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelPeriodicTuningStateEnum "PERIODIC_TUNING_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PERIODIC_TUNING_DISABLED"|"ALL_TUNING_DISABLED"|"PERIODIC_TUNING_ENABLED"

---Represents an ordered combination of valid serving configs, which can be used for `PAGE_OPTIMIZATION` recommendations.
---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelServingConfigList
---@field servingConfigIds? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.StringList Optional. A set of valid serving configs that may be used for `PAGE_OPTIMIZATION`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelServingConfigListList gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelServingConfigList[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelServingStateEnum "SERVING_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INACTIVE"|"ACTIVE"|"TUNED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaModelTrainingStateEnum "TRAINING_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PAUSED"|"TRAINING"

---The output configuration setting.
---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaOutputConfig
---@field gcsDestination? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaOutputConfigGcsDestination The Google Cloud Storage location where the output is to be written to.
---@field bigqueryDestination? gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaOutputConfigBigQueryDestination The BigQuery location where the output is to be written to.

---The BigQuery output destination configuration.
---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaOutputConfigBigQueryDestination
---@field tableIdPrefix? string Required. The prefix of exported BigQuery tables.
---@field tableType? string Required. Describes the table type. The following values are supported: * `table`: A BigQuery native table. * `view`: A virtual table defined by a SQL query.
---@field datasetId? string Required. The ID of a BigQuery Dataset.

---The Google Cloud Storage output destination configuration.
---@class gcp.unstable.retail_v2alpha.GoogleCloudRetailV2alphaOutputConfigGcsDestination
---@field outputUriPrefix? string Required. The output uri prefix for saving output data to json files. Some mapping examples are as follows: output_uri_prefix sample output(assuming the object is foo.json) ======================== ============================================= gs://bucket/ gs://bucket/foo.json gs://bucket/folder/ gs://bucket/folder/foo.json gs://bucket/folder/item_ gs://bucket/folder/item_foo.json

---Detailed panel information associated with a user event.
